    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters 2026-06-14 with a roster optimized to exploit favorable matchups against a slate of sub-par starting pitching. **Corbin Carroll** (79.46) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) headline our daily efficiency scores, providing the highest floors in the lineup. **Corbin Carroll** overcomes a slight L/L platoon disadvantage against Abbott to remain a must-start due to elite plate positioning and projected speed production, while **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits significantly from the matchup against Sugano, capitalizing on a +19% SP skill boost and a prime #3 spot in the order. **Jose Caballero** (75.83) also warrants heavy consideration, as his +13% dynamic platoon edge against Corbin makes him a sneaky high-upside play for stolen bases\u2014our most critical scarcity category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Max Muncy** (57.67), who narrowly edged out bench options but remains in the \"marginal\" tier due to his position in the bottom third of the lineup. While the optimizer looked for a reason to rotate in depth, the lack of viable alternatives due to the IL statuses of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** keeps **Max Muncy** in the MI slot by default. We are closely monitoring the environment for **Dalton Rushing** (47.18) and **Alex Freeland** (51.01); while both are hampered by the #8 and #9 spots in the lineup respectively, the wind blowing out at their venue provides a slight cushion that keeps them above the bench floor.\n\nWe are navigating a relatively clean weather outlook today, though we must remain vigilant regarding the high-leverage arm of Peralta, who poses a genuine threat to **Austin Riley** (53.34). **Austin Riley** currently sits at the edge of our starting threshold; while his raw talent is undeniable, the -4% park penalty and the difficulty of the matchup suggest he is a prime candidate to be subbed out if we encounter any defensive substitutions or mid-game adjustments. As we push for points, we remain concerned about the lack of healthy depth, as **Seiya Suzuki** is confirmed out of the lineup, leaving us thin if any of our starters are pulled early.",
